{title: Four Men in the Fire}
{subtitle: Daniel 3:1–28}
{key: Eb}
{tempo: 100}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Eb] | [Eb] | [Eb] | [Abmaj7/Eb] [Eb] |
| [Bb] | [Eb] | [Eb/G] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Eb]The [Bb]king set up a golden image high upon the plain
When the music [Ab]played the nations [Eb]bowed, they bowed and bowed again
But three [Bb]young men [Ab]stood upright when the horn began [Eb]to sound
Shadrach, Meshach, and [Ab]Abednego would not bow down
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Our [Bb]God whom we serve is ab[Eb]le to deliver us from the blazing furnace
And he [Ab]will deliver [Eb]us from your hand, O king
But [Bb]if not, know this, O [Ab]king
We [Eb]will not serve your gods
And we will not [Ab]worship the golden [Bb]image you have [Ab]set up
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Seven times [Bb]hotter roared the fire, the king was [Eb]full of rage
They bound them in their robes and turbans, threw them in the blaze
[Ab]The flames leapt out [Eb]and killed the guards who brought them to the [Bb]door
But [Ab]the king rose up astonished at [Eb]the sight he saw once more
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
Did [Ab]we not throw three men, bound, into [Bb]the fire
I see four men, [Eb]unbound, walking around in the middle of the fire
And the fourth looks [Bb]like a [Abmaj7]son of the [Eb]gods
Not a hair of their heads was singed
No smell [Ab]of fire clung to them
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Eb]Our God whom we serve [Bb]is able [Ab]to deliv[Eb]er us [Bb]from [Ab]the blazing furnace
And he [Eb]will deliver us from your hand, O king
But if not, know this, O king
We [Ab]will not serve your [Eb]gods
And we will not worship [Bb]the golden image [Ab]you have [Eb]set up
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
Blessed be the God of Shadrach, [Ab]Meshach, and Abed[Bb]nego
Who sent [Ab]his angel and res[Bb]cued his servants who trusted [Eb]in him
{end_of_verse}

{comment: Outro (instrumental)}
